# VirtForge Cloud

Multi-tenant IaaS platform native to Kubernetes: KubeVirt (VMs), Multus (networks), NetworkPolicy (security groups).

## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| API | Go 1.25 + Gorilla Mux + net/http |
| Auth | JWT (root + tenant admins) |
| Persistence | MySQL (`store.Repository`) or Memory (dev) |
| Hypervisor | KubeVirt (`internal/infra/hypervisor`) |
| K8s ops | `internal/platform/k8s` (tenants, VPCs, NADs, SGs) |
| UI | React 18 + Vite + Tailwind + TanStack Query |
| Deploy | Dockerfiles in `docker/`; cluster manifests in [virtforge-chart](https://github.com/virtforge-cloud/virtforge-chart) |

## Structure

```
cmd/server/          # REST API + WebSocket
cmd/worker/          # Async jobs (deploy_vm, reconcile)
cmd/migrate/         # CloudStack → VirtForge import
internal/api/        # Handlers, middleware, ws hub
internal/service/    # PlatformService (store + k8s + kubevirt)
internal/platform/   # Models, store, k8s manager
ui/src/              # Frontend (pages, components, lib)
```

## Multi-tenant model

- Root creates tenants; header `X-Tenant-ID` required for root to operate in a tenant
- Tenant → namespace `nimbus-tenant-{slug}`
- VPC → namespace `nimbus-vpc-{slug}-{id}` + Multus NAD
- VM → VirtualMachine in tenant namespace
- Security Group → NetworkPolicy

## OSS conventions

- Go module: `github.com/virtforge-cloud/virtforge`
- API base: `/api/v1`; WebSockets: `/ws/console`, `/ws/events`
- JSON errors: `{"error":"..."}`; helpers in `handler/common.go`
- Query keys centralized in `ui/src/lib/query-keys.ts` — keep in sync with `useRealtimeEvents`
- **Commits**: English, Conventional Commits (`feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `chore`, …)
- **Documentation**: English; extended guides on [GitHub Wiki](https://github.com/virtforge-cloud/virtforge/wiki)
- Homelab deploy: `virtforge-chart/deploy-homelab.sh`
- Helm install (production-oriented): [virtforge-cloud/virtforge-chart](https://github.com/virtforge-cloud/virtforge-chart)
